# Application-specific skills never ship in the image.
#
# `COPY sage_skills /tmp/build/skills` copies the DIRECTORY, not the tracked
# files, so anything sitting in sage_skills/ on the build host is baked in --
# including skills git never sees. A skill for one application is delivered
# with %%skill instead, from a public repo or a local path, which also keeps a
# baked copy from silently shadowing the one a notebook declares.
#
# Add a line here when a new application skill lands in sage_skills/.
sage_skills/amaro-datasets/
sage_skills/p53-dynamics/

# The wildfire review skills. Shipping them in the image was once a deliberate
# decision -- only invited reviewers were told the image tag -- and Kai reversed
# it on 2026-11-11 under the rule above. They are delivered to reviewers as a
# local path instead; the canonical copy lives outside this repo.
sage_skills/wildfire-comprehensive-report/
sage_skills/wildfire-cross-submission-report/
sage_skills/wildfire-rubric-practitioner/
sage_skills/wildfire-rubric-review/
sage_skills/wildfire-rubric-science/
